        },
        {
          "insertText": {
            "objectId": "p1_i4",
            "insertionIndex": 0,
            "text": "WETA \u00d7 Navier\nA new electric ferry layer for the San Francisco Bay\n\nSmall hydrofoiling vessels can lower the cost to serve, improve the passenger experience and open corridors that do not need a large ferry on day one.\n\nBuilt in Alameda. Designed for the Bay."
          }
        },
        {
          "deleteText": {
            "objectId": "p1_i5",
            "textRange": {
              "type": "ALL"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insertText": {
            "objectId": "p1_i5",
            "insertionIndex": 0,
            "text": "Partner discussion draft \u00b7 Passenger service first \u00b7 July 2026"
          }
        },
        {
          "deleteText": {
            "objectId": "weta_src_01",
            "textRange": {
              "type": "ALL"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insertText": {
            "objectId": "weta_src_01",
            "insertionIndex": 0,
            "text": "Sources: WETA 2050 Service Vision \u00b7 Navier N30 platform"
          }
        },
        {
          "replaceImage": {
            "imageObjectId": "p1_i2",
            "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jaideepdhanoa/navier-atlas/c2359e196ed5d569006c4a8383973b23f6f257cd/deck-studio/assets/weta/genai/weta-n30-alameda-hero-v2.png"
          }
        },
        {
          "deleteText": {
            "objectId": "p2_i3",
            "textRange": {
              "type": "ALL"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insertText": {
            "objectId": "p2_i3",
            "insertionIndex": 0,
            "text": "THE PROPOSITION\nGive WETA another way to grow service"
          }
        },
        {
          "deleteText": {
            "objectId": "p2_i4",
            "textRange": {
              "type": "ALL"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insertText": {
            "objectId": "p2_i4",
            "insertionIndex": 0,
            "text": "LOWER COST PATH\nUse less energy, reduce exposure to marine fuel and combustion-engine maintenance, and size service to demand."
          }
        },
        {
          "deleteText": {
            "objectId": "p2_i5",
            "textRange": {
              "type": "ALL"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insertText": {
            "objectId": "p2_i5",
            "insertionIndex": 0,
            "text": "MORE REACH\nAdd frequency, test an emerging market or open a new waterfront link without starting at large-ferry scale."
          }
        },
        {
          "deleteText": {
            "objectId": "p2_i6",
            "textRange": {
              "type": "ALL"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insertText": {
            "objectId": "p2_i6",
            "insertionIndex": 0,
            "text": "BETTER RIDE\nQuiet electric propulsion and active flight control create a smooth, low-wake passenger experience."
          }
        },
        {
          "deleteText": {
            "objectId": "p2_i7",
            "textRange": {
              "type": "ALL"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insertText": {
            "objectId": "p2_i7",
            "insertionIndex": 0,
            "text": "BAY-NATIVE PARTNER\nNavier is based in Alameda, close to WETA\u2019s network, terminals and operating environment."
          }
        },
        {
          "deleteText": {
            "objectId": "weta_src_02",
            "textRange": {
              "type": "ALL"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insertText": {
            "objectId": "weta_src_02",
            "insertionIndex": 0,
            "text": "Sources: WETA 2050 Service Vision \u00b7 WETA REEF \u00b7 Navier N30 platform"
          }
        },
        {
          "replaceImage": {
            "imageObjectId": "p2_i2",
            "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jaideepdhanoa/navier-atlas/c2359e196ed5d569006c4a8383973b23f6f257cd/deck-studio/assets/weta/genai/weta-n30-foil-efficiency-v2.png"
          }
        },
        {
          "deleteText": {
            "objectId": "p4_i3",
            "textRange": {
              "type": "ALL"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insertText": {
            "objectId": "p4_i3",
            "insertionIndex": 0,
            "text": "THE BAY NEEDS MORE FERRY SERVICE\nNot every trip needs the same ferry"
          }
        },
        {
          "deleteText": {
            "objectId": "p4_i5",
            "textRange": {
              "type": "ALL"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insertText": {
            "objectId": "p4_i5",
            "insertionIndex": 0,
            "text": "THE CONTEXT\n\nWETA is electrifying its fleet and advancing service in Mission Bay, Treasure Island, Berkeley and Redwood City. Large ferries are essential where demand is high.\n\nTHE PROBLEM\n\nEmerging markets can be expensive to test when each new trip begins with large vessels, major terminal work and full-scale operating commitments. Some corridors need capacity now. Others need a smaller first step."
          }
        },
        {
          "deleteText": {
            "objectId": "weta_src_03",
            "textRange": {
              "type": "ALL"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insertText": {
            "objectId": "weta_src_03",
            "insertionIndex": 0,
            "text": "Sources: WETA 2050 Service Vision \u00b7 WETA REEF program and project pages"
          }
        },
        {
          "replaceImage": {
            "imageObjectId": "p4_i2",
            "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jaideepdhanoa/navier-atlas/5a0429f27a6731bcb8813029262f8de0e12c61db/deck-studio/assets/weta/genai/weta-cover-n30-bay-v1.png"
          }
        },
        {
          "deleteText": {
            "objectId": "p3_i3",
            "textRange": {
              "type": "ALL"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insertText": {
            "objectId": "p3_i3",
            "insertionIndex": 0,
            "text": "THE N30\nA small ferry that flies above the waves"
          }
        },
        {
          "deleteText": {
            "objectId": "g3f266457366_0_1",
            "textRange": {
              "type": "ALL"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insertText": {
            "objectId": "g3f266457366_0_1",
            "insertionIndex": 0,
            "text": "RANGE\n70+ nautical miles at 20 knots."
          }
        },
        {
          "deleteText": {
            "objectId": "g3f266457366_0_2",
            "textRange": {
              "type": "ALL"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insertText": {
            "objectId": "g3f266457366_0_2",
            "insertionIndex": 0,
            "text": "SPEED\n20-knot cruise. 30-knot top speed."
          }
        },
        {
          "deleteText": {
            "objectId": "g3f266457366_0_3",
            "textRange": {
              "type": "ALL"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insertText": {
            "objectId": "g3f266457366_0_3",
            "insertionIndex": 0,
            "text": "CHARGING\nDC fast charging in approximately 45 minutes."
          }
        },
        {
          "deleteText": {
            "objectId": "g3f266457366_0_4",
            "textRange": {
              "type": "ALL"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insertText": {
            "objectId": "g3f266457366_0_4",
            "insertionIndex": 0,
            "text": "RIDE\nActive flight control adjusts up to 50 times per second."
          }
        },
        {
          "deleteText": {
            "objectId": "g3f266457366_0_6",
            "textRange": {
              "type": "ALL"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insertText": {
            "objectId": "g3f266457366_0_6",
            "insertionIndex": 0,
            "text": "HOW IT WORKS\nHydrofoils lift the hull above the waves. Electric propulsion moves it quietly. Active flight control continually adjusts the ride. Current N30 specifications; public-service configuration and operating envelope require WETA and regulatory validation."
          }
        },
        {
          "deleteText": {
            "objectId": "weta_src_04",
            "textRange": {
              "type": "ALL"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insertText": {
            "objectId": "weta_src_04",
            "insertionIndex": 0,
            "text": "Source: Navier N30 platform specifications"
          }
        },
        {
          "replaceImage": {
            "imageObjectId": "p3_i2",
            "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jaideepdhanoa/navier-atlas/c2359e196ed5d569006c4a8383973b23f6f257cd/deck-studio/assets/weta/genai/weta-n30-foil-efficiency-v2.png"
          }
        },
        {
          "deleteText": {
            "objectId": "p6_i3",
            "textRange": {
              "type": "ALL"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insertText": {
            "objectId": "p6_i3",
            "insertionIndex": 0,
            "text": "WHY THE COST TO SERVE CAN FALL\n\nLESS DRAG \u00b7 The hull flies above the chop, reducing water resistance and energy demand.\n\nELECTRIC POWER \u00b7 Less exposure to marine fuel and combustion-engine maintenance.\n\nRIGHT-SIZED SERVICE \u00b7 Add trips and capacity in smaller increments as demand develops.\n\nSOFTWARE PATH \u00b7 Remote monitoring now; autonomy can lower cost further over time, subject to certification and WETA approval.\n\nThe savings should come from vessel physics and operating design\u2014not from weaker public-service standards. Route-specific economics must be validated before procurement."
          }
        },
        {
          "updateTextStyle": {
            "objectId": "p6_i3",
            "style": {
              "fontFamily": "Poppins",
              "fontSize": {
                "magnitude": 12.1,
                "unit": "PT"
              }
