        {
          "insertText": {
            "objectId": "weta_src_08",
            "insertionIndex": 0,
            "text": "Source: WETA 2050 Service Vision and Expansion Policy"
          }
        },
        {
          "replaceImage": {
            "imageObjectId": "g3f266457366_0_11",
            "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jaideepdhanoa/navier-atlas/5a0429f27a6731bcb8813029262f8de0e12c61db/deck-studio/assets/weta/genai/weta-oakland-alameda-n30-v1.png"
          }
        },
        {
          "deleteText": {
            "objectId": "p12_i3",
            "textRange": {
              "type": "ALL"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insertText": {
            "objectId": "p12_i3",
            "insertionIndex": 0,
            "text": "START WITH MARKETS WETA ALREADY KNOWS\n\nMISSION BAY + TREASURE ISLAND \u00b7 WETA\u2019s REEF program identifies new electric service to Downtown San Francisco. Screen Navier as a feeder or added-frequency option.\n\nREDWOOD CITY \u00b7 WETA is advancing design and environmental review for San Francisco and Oakland markets. Evaluate a smaller service increment alongside the planned network.\n\nALAMEDA + OAKLAND \u00b7 Navier is based in Alameda, inside WETA\u2019s operating geography. Local demonstration and service learning can begin close to engineering and support.\n\nThese are screening areas, not route, terminal or procurement commitments."
          }
        },
        {
          "updateTextStyle": {
            "objectId": "p12_i3",
            "style": {
              "fontFamily": "Poppins",
              "fontSize": {
